WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:04.300
(happy music)

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.674
- So you're just gonna like pay someone

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:09.390
to come over and hang out with your cats?

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:11.180
- Yeah, they can't take
care of themselves.

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:12.430
- Well, why don't you just let 'em go

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:14.730
and hang out with the neighborhood cats?

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:16.480
They'll form like a Lion King.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:17.770
- They're gentle cats Calen,

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:21.140
they can't survive on the outside.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.193
Isn't that right Mr. Harris?

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.240
- How did his face get
all smushed like that?

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:29.990
- That's the breed, they're
supposed to look like that.

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:32.160
- Oh, so you didn't
like raise him in a jar

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.500
like one of those Japanese
cubed watermelons?

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.460
- No Calen, cats cannot grow in jars.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:39.790
I did not do that.

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:40.750
- If I had a cat I'd want him

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.330
to just be a furry cube with legs.

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:45.010
(knocking)

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:47.390
- Oh that's one of the
people that answered my ad.

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:49.930
- Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa, what are you doing?

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:53.470
- I'm gonna be gone for a week,
it's already getting sour.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.940
- Please, you go do the interview,

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:58.093
let me worry about the food.

00:00:58.093 --> 00:00:59.980
- All right, you're not
gonna drink it are you?

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:00.900
- No.

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:05.150
- I see you have degrees
in cat and dog behavior.

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:07.160
- It's important to know the enemy.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:10.450
- True, there's a war brewing
with the dog community.

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:12.330
What is your experience with problem cats?

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:14.950
Mr. Harris has two strikes
with the humane society.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:18.170
- Mr. Harris, come.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.670
- Wow.

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:25.630
He doesn't usually respond to English.

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:26.510
Impressive, Albert.

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:28.090
(knocking)

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:30.350
Excuse me for just a second.

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:34.890
- Hi, I'm Jenny.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:36.480
- Oh, hi.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.650
- I'm here for the cat-sitter interview.

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:40.650
- Oh right, Jenny.

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:43.360
Hi I'm Elliott, nice to meet you.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:44.820
- Nice to meet you.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:46.700
- Uh, you're here early though.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:49.070
- Oh, I can come back later.

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:50.510
- No, no, you should stay.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:51.450
- [Jenny] Okay.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:52.280
- Just give me a second.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:52.990
- Sure.

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:54.320
- One sec, just--

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:54.960
- [Jenny] Okay.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.694
- I'm sorry, one second.

00:01:57.694 --> 00:01:59.450
Hey Albert this is Calen,

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:01.460
he's Britney Purrs's cat godfather.

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:03.493
- Hey, don't call me that.

00:02:03.493 --> 00:02:04.880
- Yeah, so why don't you guys hang out

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:06.750
and talk about cats for a while?

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:07.550
You love cats, right?

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:08.660
Okay, bye.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:11.970
- Hey, you know that show Cat Dog?

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:14.260
You ever seen one of those?

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.140
I have.

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:18.720
- So you're an actress living in L.A.?

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.650
- Yeah, it's been okay.

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:22.730
I do a lot of side gigs
to keep the lights on.

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:26.140
- Oh yeah, I bet, like dealing drugs and--

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:27.490
- Oh yeah, yeah.

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:29.604
Heroin, meth, coke.

00:02:29.604 --> 00:02:30.860
- Oh my god, really?

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:33.070
- No, no, no, I'm totally kidding.

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:34.700
- Oh, right (laughs).

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.524
Yeah cool, cool, super cool.

00:02:36.524 --> 00:02:38.540
So, do you like cats?

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:39.540
- Mmm hmmm, yeah.

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:41.210
I have a cat, Banjo.

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:43.750
He's a little shy, but super sweet.

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:44.960
- Oh, that's great.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:47.340
And have you ever cat-sat?

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:49.380
- No.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:56.393
- Albert's the clear choice,
but something about Jenny.

00:02:56.393 --> 00:02:57.720
- You can just say you like her.

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:59.060
- Is it unethical to hire someone

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:00.380
because you wanna date them?

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:03.600
- No, I mean I went out
with my probation officer.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.020
- You're a terrible person.

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:06.820
- I'm a great person.

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:08.280
- You have a probation officer.

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:10.240
- Elliott, I'd expect you
of all people not to buy

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:13.240
into America's prison industrial complex.

00:03:14.853 --> 00:03:18.080
- I just, I wanna know my
cats are gonna be okay.

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:19.696
I need to hire the best person.

00:03:19.696 --> 00:03:21.960
- I mean, you can really
do whatever you want.

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:23.960
I kinda don't care anymore.

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:25.210
- Yeah, you're right.

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:26.630
I'm gonna move on to phase 2.

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:27.210
- Sure.

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:30.760
- Okay, it's time for
Britney Purrs's pill,

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:32.040
how do you give it to her?

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:35.550
- Insert the capsule into an
edible pill pocket, place it

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:39.140
in her mouth and gently
massage it down her throat.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:41.300
- Just hide it in some
delicious human food.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:42.270
- I love human food.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:44.560
- Human food often contains spices

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:46.980
which are poisonous to cats.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:49.110
- That is true.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:52.190
Next question, Mr. Harris is
sitting in the loaf position

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:55.410
on the couch and will
not move, what do you do?

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:57.870
- Awww, well first take a
photo because that's too cute.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:00.910
- Loafing can be a sign of stress.

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:02.620
I would have to call the vet.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:04.420
- All right, next question.

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:07.000
Britney Purrs has mild hemorrhoids,

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.786
what happens when she can't move

00:04:08.786 --> 00:04:10.840
due to the burning sensation?

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:12.800
- With me at all times.

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:14.250
- Are those clinical strength?

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:15.640
- Indeed.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:19.430
- Welcome to the free-form
section of the interview process.

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:23.180
So, how would you describe
their fantasy island?

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:26.683
- It'd be a little island
with just this house in it.

00:04:26.683 --> 00:04:27.556
- That's it?

00:04:27.556 --> 00:04:30.150
- You'd be in it, all the time.

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:32.770
You'd never go to work.

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:35.700
Because you're their whole universe.

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.064
(laughs)

00:04:38.214 --> 00:04:39.200
- Yeah.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.523
Thank you for coming, Albert.

00:04:41.523 --> 00:04:43.410
But, I'll see ya.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:45.620
Good luck with your hemorrhoid
ointments and all that.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:46.910
Okay, bye.

00:04:47.615 --> 00:04:49.034
- Thank you so much.

00:04:49.034 --> 00:04:49.730
- Thank you.

00:04:49.730 --> 00:04:50.880
- I'll see you next Friday.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:52.540
- Yes, please, I can't wait.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:53.720
- [Jenny] Yeah, bye.

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:54.920
- Bye.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:58.430
- Did you ask her out?

00:04:58.430 --> 00:04:59.890
- No, not yet.

00:04:59.890 --> 00:05:01.850
- And, you're not going to.

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:03.220
- Probably not, I'm terrified.

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:04.810
- Yeah.

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:07.350
Cat threw up on your bed.

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:11.320
- [Elliott] But my cats can't throw up.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:19.370
Did you drink all their milk?

